Testing: SDD

Purpose:
  Testing technology catalog with framework options, selection criteria,
  and integration patterns. Root stack/ defines reusable testing knowledge;
  instances/vkard.az/stack/ stores the selected testing stack for the project.

Catalog:
  Playwright:
    Type: E2E / Integration
    Pros:
      - Multi-browser support
      - Multi-language (TS, JS, Python, Java, C#)
      - Auto-wait
      - Trace viewer
      - Parallel execution
    Cons:
      - Steeper learning curve than Cypress
      - Heavier setup
    BestFor:
      - Cross-browser E2E testing
      - Complex user flows
      - API testing
    AvoidWhen:
      - Simple component testing
    Integration:
      - Works with all major frameworks
      - CI/CD friendly

  Cypress:
    Type: E2E / Component
    Pros:
      - Excellent DX
      - Time-travel debugging
      - Automatic waiting
      - Component testing
    Cons:
      - JavaScript/TypeScript only
      - Multi-tab limitations
      - No native mobile support
    BestFor:
      - Frontend E2E testing
      - Component testing
      - Teams new to testing
    AvoidWhen:
      - Multi-browser needs
      - API-heavy testing

  Vitest:
    Type: Unit / Integration
    Pros:
      - Vite-native
      - Fast execution
      - ESM support
      - Jest-compatible API
    Cons:
      - Newer framework
      - Smaller ecosystem
    BestFor:
      - Vite projects
      - Fast unit testing
      - Modern JS/TS projects
    AvoidWhen:
      - Legacy Webpack projects

  Jest:
    Type: Unit / Integration
    Pros:
      - Mature ecosystem
      - Large community
      - Snapshot testing
      - Good documentation
    Cons:
      - Slower than Vitest
      - Configuration complexity
    BestFor:
      - Mature projects
      - Snapshot testing
      - React projects
    AvoidWhen:
      - New projects (prefer Vitest)

  Go testing:
    Type: Unit / Integration
    Pros:
      - Built-in
      - Fast execution
      - Table-driven tests
      - Benchmark support
    Cons:
      - No mocking built-in
      - Verbose assertions
    BestFor:
      - Go projects
      - High-performance testing
    AvoidWhen:
      - Complex mocking needs

  PHPUnit:
    Type: Unit / Integration
    Pros:
      - Mature ecosystem
      - Laravel integration
      - Code coverage
    Cons:
      - Slower execution
      - XML configuration
    BestFor:
      - PHP projects
      - Laravel testing
    AvoidWhen:
      - Non-PHP projects

SelectionRules:
  - ProjectType: frontend, backend, mobile, full-stack
  - TeamFit: existing testing expertise
  - CI/CD: integration with CI pipeline
  - Reporting: test reporting requirements
  - Coverage: code coverage requirements
  - Speed: test execution speed requirements

TechnologyScore:
  ProjectType: 0-25
  TeamFit: 0-20
  CICD: 0-15
  Reporting: 0-10
  Coverage: 0-15
  Speed: 0-15

State: +
  